      "94": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "EXAMPLE 1: RADIUS SLIDER\nIn this example we've created a Float In node to control the radius of the Circle.\nThe min is set to 0 and the max to 1, so we end up with a slider running from 0 to 1."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 266.89996337890625,
          "width": 678.318115234375,
          "x": 133.67489624023438,
          "y": -424.7564392089844
        },
        "class": {
          "id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
          "version": 1
        },
        "clock": "video",
        "color": "ffff6a00",
        "constants": {},
        "hidden": [
          "text",
          "alignment",
          "font-size",
          "fill"
        ],
        "name": "Comment"
      },
      "95": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "EXAMPLE 2: FREQUENCY INPUT\n\nIn this example we've removed the min and max bounds and changed the unit to Hertz."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 301.1493835449219,
          "width": 912.1589965820312,
          "x": 133.67489624023438,
          "y": -122.41668701171876
        },
        "class": {
          "id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
          "version": 1
        },
        "clock": "video",
        "color": "ff02bbff",
        "constants": {},
        "hidden": [
          "text",
          "alignment",
          "font-size",
          "fill"
        ],
        "name": "Comment"
      },
      "96": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "EXAMPLE 3: FLOAT TO TEXTURE\n\nIn this example we have 4 Float In nodes named Red, Green, Blue and Alpha.\nWe've set the unit to percent and set the range from 0 to 100.\nBut to construct a color we need a value from 0 to 1.\nThis is why we divide by 100 again.\nThis is something you will do often, a slider might run from 0 to 100 in the interface, but in the patch it gets converted back to 0 to 1.\nNodes like Map and 1-x are useful for this purpose too."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 628.2904052734375,
          "width": 1155.447998046875,
          "x": 133.67489624023438,
          "y": 192.91421508789062
        },
        "class": {
          "id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
          "version": 1
        },
        "clock": "video",
        "color": "ff20c7bb",
        "constants": {},
        "hidden": [
          "text",
          "alignment",
          "font-size",
          "fill"
        ],
        "name": "Comment"
      },
      "97": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "EXAMPLE 4: PULSES\n\nIn this example we are creating a video oscillator from a single Sine oscillator.\nWe use a Float In node, named Pulses, that runs from 1 to 8 at attribute flow.\nThis sets the max of the Linear node up to set the Phase Offset of the Sine."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 500.7340087890625,
          "width": 1702.2972412109375,
          "x": 133.04788208007812,
          "y": 850.7479248046875
        },
        "class": {
          "id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
          "version": 1
        },
        "clock": "video",
        "color": "ffe53357",
        "constants": {},
        "hidden": [
          "text",
          "alignment",
          "font-size",
          "fill"
        ],
        "name": "Comment"
      },
      "98": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": true
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "FLOAT IN\n\nThe Float Input node creates an input slider that sends out a floating point number.\nIf the Float Input has either its min and max disabled in the node panel, the slider disappears and becomes an input box.\nBecause this is an input node, the slider or box will appear in the Dashboard panel and in the Arena/Avenue interface.\n\nIf you need to construct or convert a float, you should use the Float node instead."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 163.95333862304688,
          "width": 678.0775146484375,
          "x": 132.730224609375,
          "y": -612.9750366210938
        },
